-*   **Strengths:** Adaptive resolution allows for high detail where needed and coarser resolution elsewhere. Dual contouring with QEF solving can handle complex topologies and sharp features better than linear interpolation methods.
-*   **Limitations:** QEF solving is computationally more expensive than linear interpolation. The recursive nature may lead to high memory usage for deep octrees.
-*   **When to use:** When high-fidelity surface reconstruction is required from volumetric data with varying density, and manifold connectivity is critical.
-*   **When not:** When real-time performance is critical and the volume is uniform, or when the volume is too large for the octree structure to fit in memory.
